human_review:
[aten/src/ATen/native/mps/operations/GridSampler.mm] `at::Tensor::contiguous()` returns `&this` if tensor is already contiguous, so this ternaries are superflous
```suggestion
  const auto& input_contiguous = input.contiguous();
  const auto& grid_contiguous = grid.contiguous();
  const auto& grad_output_contiguous = grad_output.contiguous();
```

[aten/src/ATen/native/mps/kernels/GridSampler.metal] Actually, I guess you could do just one loop. Something like this should work I think:

```
for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
    auto x_pair_idx = i & 1;
    auto y_pair_idx = (i & 2) >> 1;
    auto z_pair_idx = (i & 4) >> 2;
    ...
}
```

