[aten/src/ATen/native/sparse/SparseFactories.cpp] I was working on a fix too until I noticed this PR. Thanks for taking this up!

I have a slightly different implementation of this that might a bit more efficient as it avoids creating too many temporaries. Here's what I had:

```cpp
  // The number of non-zero elements in each diagonal is determined by two
  // factors; the size of that diagonal and the number of elements available
  // to fill that diagonal.
  //
  // If the size of the target matrix is (R, C) then the size of diagonal at
  // index i is given by min(R, R+i, C, C-i).
  //
  // If the columns in the diagonals matrix is D, the number of elements
  // available to fill the diagonal at index i is given by D - max(i, 0)
  // because we skip first i elements for positive indices.
  //
  // Taking both these factors into account the final number of non-zero
  // elements per diagonal is: min(R, R+i, C, C-i, D, D-i). This can be
  // broken down into cases as follows and then simplified:
  //
  // i <= 0  -> min(R+i, min(C, D))
  // i >= 0  -> min(R, min(C,D)-i)
  //            = min(R+i, min(C,D)) - i
  //
  // Combining: min(R+i, min(C, D)) - max(i, 0)
  //
  auto nnz_per_diag = offsets_1d.add(shape[0])
    .clamp_max_(std::min<int64_t>(shape[1], diagonals_2d.size(1)))
    .sub_(offsets_1d.clamp_min(0));
```

Feel free to incorporate this into the PR if the implementation makes sense and passes your tests.

