[torch/csrc/Module.cpp] Currently, `c10::Stream` already has a unified method `native_handle` in https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/2055be532acdf7840544fa3be1567d47cdbbc7c6/c10/core/Stream.h#L118. So here we could do like this:
```cpp
    if (at::accelerator::getAccelerator() && (device_type == kDLCUDA || device_type == kDLROCM || device_type == kDLoneAPI)) {
         *out_stream = at::accelerator::getCurrentStream(device_id).native_handle();
    }
```
One more thing—I think we should add a test case to ensure:
1. intended usage of this API, and
2. correctness of this code change.
